---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets'
import { hero4 } from '../../assets'

const photo = await getImage({ src: hero4, width: 600, format: 'webp', quality: 80 })
---

<div id="about" class="p-div c_container">
  <section class="about-me">
    <div class="about-c">
      <div class="c-bio-title">
        <h1 class="bio-title">About Me</h1>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bio">
      <div class="c-bio-img">
        <img
          src={photo.src}
          alt="Portrait of Fernando Solorzano"
          class="bio-img"
          width="100"
          height="100"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="c-bio-text">
        <p class="bio-text">
          I’m a <b>software engineer</b> with <b>2+ years of experience</b> building web apps that
          work well and look good doing it.
        </p>
        <p class="bio-text">
          I’m into learning new stuff, cracking tricky problems, and turning random ideas into things
          people actually use.
        </p>
        <p class="bio-text">
          <b>If you can dream it up, I can build it.</b>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hide-text">
      <p>
        I like building useful, scalable tools: anything from small web projects to automation and AI
        experiments. Whether it’s a side project or part of a bigger product, I keep things simple and
        clean.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/#contact"><b>Let’s build something cool together.</b></a>
      </p>
      <p>
        When I’m not coding, I’m hooping. Basketball taught me that having a game plan makes all the
        difference, and the same goes for writing good code.
      </p>
      <ul class="nes-list is-circle hide-list">
        <li class="hide-list-item">
          Always picking up new tech and trying out ideas to level up my craft.
        </li>
        <li class="hide-list-item">
          I write poems sometimes; it helps me reset and see things from a different angle.
        </li>
        <li class="hide-list-item">
          Lately I’ve been nerding out on <b>machine learning</b> and AI projects, just for fun (and
          out of pure curiosity).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
